<title>SWEDEN: Saab U.S. car sales tumble 37 pct in October.</title>
<headline>Saab U.S. car sales tumble 37 pct in October.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish vehicle maker Saab Automobile said on Monday its U.S. car sales fell 37 percent in October to 1,478 units.</p>
<p>So far this year Saab has sold six percent more cars in the U.S. compared to the first 10 months in 1995 with a total 24,053 vehicles sold, Saab Automobile spokesman Olof Wallen told Reuters.</p>
